steps.text:
Protein is the only macronutrient with much nitrogen. So tracking nitrogen tracks protein. Food protein is usually estimated as nitrogen × **6.25** (protein is about 16% nitrogen) [[c:pro-625]].

[Nitrogen balance](g:nitrogen-balance) compares the nitrogen eaten with the nitrogen lost in urine, faeces and sweat [[c:pro-nbal-def]]:

- **positive**: the body is gaining protein (growth, building muscle);
- **zero**: intake matches losses;
- **negative**: the body is losing protein, which impairs recovery.

Using this method, elite endurance athletes needed about 1.67 times as much protein as sedentary people to stay in balance; the authors put it down to protein burned in training [[c:pro-tarno]]. How much protein to eat each day is for *Protein and recovery*.
